::ALG2_U05_L03_GP_Q01::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L03_GP_Q01<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.SYS.4<br><br>Question:<br>Solve y=x<sup>2</sup> and y=4. {
= (-2,4) and (2,4)#Correct. Set x<sup>2</sup>=4, so x=-2 or x=2.
~ (4,16)#This is on the parabola but not y=4.
~ (0,4)#This is on y=4 but not on the parabola.
~ (2,2)#This is not on y=4.
}

::ALG2_U05_L03_GP_Q02::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L03_GP_Q02<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.SYS.4<br><br>Question:<br>Solve y=x<sup>2</sup> and y=x+2. {
~ (1,3)#This point is on the line but not the parabola.
= (-1,1) and (2,4)#Correct. Set x<sup>2</sup>=x+2 and factor x<sup>2</sup>-x-2.
~ (0,2)#This point is on the line but not the parabola.
~ No solution#The graphs intersect twice.
}

::ALG2_U05_L03_GP_Q03::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L03_GP_Q03<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.SYS.4<br><br>Question:<br>If x represents time, which solution should be rejected? {
~ x=0#Zero time can be meaningful as an initial time.
~ x=3#Positive time can be meaningful.
= x=-2#Correct. Negative time is not meaningful in this context.
~ x=8#Positive time can be meaningful.
}

::ALG2_U05_L03_GP_Q04::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L03_GP_Q04<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.SYS.4<br><br>Question:<br>What does a solution of a nonlinear system represent graphically? {
~ Only a vertex#A vertex may or may not be an intersection.
~ Only a y-intercept#Intersections can occur anywhere.
~ A point outside both graphs#That cannot satisfy both equations.
= An intersection point#Correct. A solution is a point shared by all graphs.
}

::ALG2_U05_L03_GP_Q05::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L03_GP_Q05<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.SYS.4<br><br>Question:<br>Which point satisfies y=x<sup>2</sup> and y=2x? {
= (0,0) and (2,4)#Correct. Set x<sup>2</sup>=2x, so x=0 or x=2.
~ (1,2)#This satisfies y=2x but not y=x<sup>2</sup>.
~ (2,2)#This satisfies neither equation fully.
~ No solution#The graphs intersect twice.
}

